WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.800
[Music]

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.800
We're fourth-generation farmers
from Mildura.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.800
My grandfather and great-grandfather,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.460
and dad, have all been involved
in farming this way.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:18.870
Dad bought these farms in this region
back in 1969 and started his own business

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:19.560
from there.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.810
Around the late '80s, he was having
some problems with soil compaction,

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.920
and just a decline in the trees
and so forth.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.560
His sister pointed him
towards biodynamic farming.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.600
The first farm was certified biodynamic
in 1989,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.560
Since then, it's been a lifestyle
and philosophy we've run with.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.200
It's now my brother Rob and myself
who own and run the business.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:48.840
In 2009, I suppose we were probably
somewhere around 550, 600 acres.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:54.230
Over the following three years,
we expanded and expanded and expanded,

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:59.910
and we've ended up now with 1,300 acres:
just under 400 acres of citrus,

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.560
around 500 acres of almonds,
15 acres of avocados,

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.110
and this big beast
of a biodynamic farming operation.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.160
We just want to produce
the best-quality fruit we can,

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.560
whether organic, conventional
or biodynamic.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.810
It's all about taste and flavour.
Producing a nice, nutrient-dense fruit

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:19.840
probably relates to eating quality.
The better the fruit tastes,

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:23.560
that's going to bring return customers
and drive profitability in the business.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.800
As the farming industry changes,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.660
people want to know this
paddock-to-plate stuff.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.560
They want to get in touch and in contact
with who it is that's growing their fruit,

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.950
what their properties look like,
and be actively involved

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.560
or emotionally tied
to the actual farm itself.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.560
Regenerative farming
will matter more,

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.560
looking after the soil
and being potentially carbon neutral.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.200
People will drive and push us as farmers
to look after the land a lot better

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.560
than what we have.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.560
Climate change is obviously
a massive issue.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.560
Farming is probably one industry
that can fix it straight away,

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.560
if we really wanted to,
across the world.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:02.300
We originally brought them on board
around 2011, I think it was.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:06.560
The main reason was a change in some
of the composting we were using.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.150
We were putting out straight cow manure,

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.800
and quite a lot of it.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.400
We talked to Hybrid Ag
about what they could do for us,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.800
We found a few tweaks
in the compost blend

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.100
could significantly reduce the amount

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.560
we were putting out.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.610
So we decided to give it a go,
and we did see some great results

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.560
straight up.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.500
That relationship's only grown,

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.590
especially over the last three
or four years.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:33.430
Tom and I often sit down in the office
and have a bit of a chinwag about life,

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:38.560
philosophies about farming,
and what we should be doing

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.500
to look after the land and the soil,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.560
and leave it better
than we started.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.720
Having that trust with him,
and what he believes,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.830
That gives us the flexibility
to let him take charge of some areas,

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.560
and areas we're not happy with.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.560
It's a nice, smooth, easy relationship.
It's happy days from my point of view.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.500
[Music]

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.560
Hybrid Ag. Transforming food for health.
